13:55:33.895 world 0 channel 0 listening on 127.0.0.1:8485
13:55:33.895 database C:\MapleCW\maplecw.db
13:55:33.895 NOT AUTHENTICATED: a migration seed is a u32, so it identifies a pending
13:55:33.895   migration rather than proving who is on the far end. It is single-use.
13:55:33.895 SET-FIELD PROBE IS ON - which by now means 'the channel answers at all'. The
13:55:33.895   flag is a misnomer kept for the launch line: without it Session::handle
13:55:33.896   returns nothing for every packet, so the migration hello goes unanswered and
13:55:33.896   the client freezes on 'Connecting...'.
13:55:33.896   With it on, this channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
13:55:33.896   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
13:55:33.896   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
13:55:33.896   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
13:55:33.896   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
13:55:33.896   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
13:55:33.896   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
13:55:33.896   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
13:55:33.896   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
